e years but this one is definitely the best.","this 1 series is my first ever bmw and i'm really impressed with the power, the fuel economy and how comfortable it is. the amount of standard kit is great, and the safety features make me feel confident and are a big help, especially when parking. the seats are extremely comfortable and the cabin is very quiet, so it is a very enjoyable car to drive. the materials used inside feel high quality and the os9 instruments are very detailed with lots of different display options. i would happily recommend the 1 series and i expect to stay with bmw for many years.","the mild hybrid start feels subtle.\r\nthere are too many separate safety systems.\r\nfrequent stops when refueling. etc","my car broke down and i couldnt get it started again, after roughly two months and about 3000kms on the clock. quite penalizing for someone investing in a new car for safety, expecting no nasty surprises!","for me at 70, the safety and driving systems in the car are excellent. they let you drive feeling relaxed and give both physical and mental comfort. the fuel economy was better than i expected as well, at 23.6 km/l over roughly 500 km of high speed driving.\r\nyou can really enjoy the pleasure of driving it.\r\nbeing compact it's simple to wash, and overall it's just the right car for my current car life.","it feels very secure and stable to drive, so it is really comfortable in terms of safety and handling. especially, i use the autonomous driving feature with a lot of confidence."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0003","F70-0042","F70-0054","F70-0176","F70-0191","F70-0202","F70-0218","F70-0234","F70-0298","F70-0347","F70-0349","F70-0373","F70-0437","F70-0478","F70-0499","F70-0500","F70-0536","F70-0659","F70-0665","F70-0730","F70-0763","F70-0773","F70-0788","F70-0850","F70-0902","F70-0903","F70-0932","F70-0973","F70-0982","F70-1014"],"countries":{"GB":22,"JP":31,"FR":2,"SE":4}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"steering","theme":"Drive, driving dynamics and chassis, overall technology","frequency":475,"likes":475,"wants":0,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":0,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["i've always been a big fan of the brand, starting with my first bmw, a used e46 320i coupe back in 2007, then an e83 x3 2.5i, before working in the bmw retailer network as a parts manager and later an aftersales manager, driving lots of company cars over the years, my favourite being the g21 m340d. after getting my wife an f56 cooper sport as her first car a couple of years ago, when it was time to change, the new 1 series was the obvious choice. she absolutely loves it and now understands why i've always said bmw will always be the best brand. james and the team at northbridge bmw chester wer","overall the car is very good, drives nicely, feels comfortable and looks smart. however, using the touch screen for various controls is awkward and far too complicated. the car actually broke down in the first two weeks of ownership and then needed nearly three weeks to be repaired, which is very disappointing for a new vehicle and below what i'd expect from bmw.","looks superb, great driveability and performance, good economy, and the interior comfort with the m front seats. the options i picked when buying plus the driver aids all help, i really enjoy driving this car.","the car is fantastic to drive. it's my first automatic and it's incredibly easy to use. i'm very happy with it.","the car drives very well and has some lovely features, however i've had problems with both display modules going totally blank several times, always when the outside temperature is under zero degrees. the vehicle is currently with the local dealer for checks and repair.","this is my 4th bmw 1 series and easily the best to drive. the mild hybrid setup is excellent, same with the automatic gearbox. i have already done around a 1000 mile round trip to france in great comfort and with superb fuel economy."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0004","F70-0018","F70-0021","F70-0025","F70-0027","F70-0028","F70-0030","F70-0040","F70-0053","F70-0064","F70-0075","F70-0080","F70-0089","F70-0092","F70-0093","F70-0098","F70-0099","F70-0106","F70-0108","F70-0115","F70-0121","F70-0123","F70-0127","F70-0133","F70-0136","F70-0147","F70-0151","F70-0156","F70-0160","F70-0161"],"countries":{"GB":355,"JP":74,"SE":21,"FR":13,"DK":6,"FI":3,"ZA":1,"AU":2}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"steering","theme":"Driver assistance, automated driving, overall technology","frequency":39,"likes":20,"wants":4,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":15,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["offers a great balance of comfort and sport, ideal for anyone wanting that mix.\r\ni do feel the assist motor power could be just a bit stronger!","after my husband changed his phone he has not been able to load the bmw app, and even though he has asked for help he just keeps getting passed around. on the day we collected the car it was not ready because they had sprayed the roof black as they could not secure the car we had been promised. we did not get a proper hand over as we were anxious about picking up primary schoolchildren and had told the garage we would have to go. about 5 or 6 weeks later we needed an emergency technician and the car had to return to the garage because the gps in the roof fin had been damaged by rain, so the ro","fantastic car, econmical and reliable, great to drive and i really like the safety features and tech.","i picked the bmw 120 m sport because in this segment it seemed the best overall mix of equipment and value for money. it looks sharp, feels very refined and is straightforward to drive, with a solid quality feel. performance is strong, and both fuel economy and emissions are impressive. the interior finish is high quality, the seats are very comfortable, and the infotainment is wide ranging yet simple to use. features like parking assist and the other safety tech are handy and easy to set up. so far the car has been very easy to live with, with no faults or reliability issues.","i'm very happy with the high-speed stability, the fuel economy, the safety features, the heated seats and all that. i changed over from a 116i i purchased in 2014, and the level of luxury now feels so much higher it barely seems like the same one series.","absolutely love this car!! nice and compact, really simple to park thanks to the parking assist. the speed limit warnings are helpful, and it's very easy to drive, smooth on the road."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0005","F70-0085","F70-0149","F70-0203","F70-0270","F70-0327","F70-0346","F70-0361","F70-0381","F70-0410","F70-0521","F70-0535","F70-0572","F70-0616","F70-0629","F70-0662","F70-0697","F70-0782","F70-0801","F70-0943","F70-0996","F70-1016","F70-1117","F70-1154","F70-1179","F70-1191","F70-1221","F70-1257","F70-1402","F70-1520"],"countries":{"JP":10,"GB":29}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"steering","theme":"Handling / Riding","frequency":216,"likes":179,"wants":21,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":16,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["i was driving a golf 7.5 before and felt it was more stable and better to operate than local cars, but the 120 takes stability even further. i can tell that its rigidity and its quietness are key parts of those fundamentals.","you travel nicely, with safety and a luxurios feel.","its compact but comfy to ride in and really easy to drive","the ride is supposed to be comfortable, and it mostly is. however, i felt the sunlight ought to be reduced a bit more.","even with the easy handling, you still really feel the fun that comes from riding a bmw.","the size and the way it handles feel spot on, and its running performance is the best. it fits 5 people, and i think it is the best option as long as you are ok with the firm ride and not taking big luggage."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0007","F70-0016","F70-0020","F70-0024","F70-0044","F70-0051","F70-0058","F70-0074","F70-0076","F70-0077","F70-0096","F70-0101","F70-0102","F70-0113","F70-0129","F70-0132","F70-0135","F70-0158","F70-0159","F70-0182","F70-0189","F70-0200","F70-0214","F70-0215","F70-0228","F70-0242","F70-0249","F70-0254","F70-0256","F70-0257"],"countries":{"JP":142,"SE":2,"FI":1,"GB":71}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"engine","theme":"Automatic engine start-stop function (MSA)","frequency":13,"likes":4,"wants":1,"difficultToUse":3,"defect":5,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["very good to drive and the extra driver safety tech is very useful. the only frustration is not being able to turn off auto stop start for good, i have to cancel it on every start. please advise if there is a way to set this permanently. thanks","the car is really enjoyable to drive and nice to sit in. everything works properly and i am pleased with the fuel economy. only small complaint is the auto stop/start feels too sensitive and cuts in too early. otherwise i am very happy.","the automatic start-stop has definitly been improved compared to the earlier model.","for me this is the best 1 series so far, theres plenty of power to have some fun, or you can just stick it in eco and save fuel. i really like the boost feature when you need to overtake quickly. i recently had the app updated and now i can deactivate the stop start through it, which makes it so much easier. up to now my only real concern is that with the lights set to auto the high beam sometimes doesnt switch off quick enough when a car is coming towards me. ive taken out the five year service plan and i love the car, really looking forward to enjoying it and having some fun times with it ov","annoying that the start/stop override can only be changed in the infotainment now. every trip i have to switch off lane departure and the speed limit warning again, really spoils it. the thin vents make the ventilation loud with wind noise. audio system not working with carplay is also very irritating.","overall it is a better, if slightly mixed, step up from my old 180i msport. the roadholding is more precise, the ride is improved on bad surfaces, there is a useful bit of extra power, the stop/start is far superior (the previous one was so poor i never used it), fuel economy is better and the engine runs smoother. on the downside, there is no single, easy-to-find autohold button anymore, it now needs one button then a touch on the screen. i rely on autohold for most driving, except for slow manoeuvres in tight areas where the throttle blip to release autohold can create more movement than i w"],"feedbackIds":["F70-0008","F70-0420","F70-0760","F70-1020","F70-1082","F70-1227","F70-1276","F70-1307","F70-1517","F70-1619","F70-2050","F70-2052","F70-2084"],"countries":{"GB":10,"JP":3}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"general","theme":"Vehicle safety, overall technology","frequency":17,"likes":17,"wants":0,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":0,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["very good to drive and the extra driver safety tech is very useful. the only frustration is not being able to turn off auto stop start for good, i have to cancel it on every start. please advise if there is a way to set this permanently. thanks","the driving performance is nearly good, but the ride comfort has a bit of a downside (the car reacts too sharply to bumps and uneven road surfaces, and the vibration comes straight through. i feel it has become worse compared with the 3 series and 5 series, and i would like that to be improved. ).\r\nthe safe driving functions are upgraded and very good. the connection to my mobile phone works well and it is handy to check the vehicle status when doing a recording or when the car is parked beforehand, but when i drive for about half a day the driving record does not transfer to the phone, which ","because the safety systems and the driving assistance functions are current and up to date.","the technology pack realy helps out, it assists and makes both parking and reversing much safer and easier.","reasonably priced with up-to-date tech, compact and easy to handle in japan, with good everyday usability and safety.","very pleasant to drive, with lots of features that really add to both comfort and safety. it feels significantly more powerful than my last 1 series even though the engine size is the same. the car looks really classy and smart overall."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0008","F70-0177","F70-0210","F70-0225","F70-0365","F70-0541","F70-0544","F70-0749","F70-0779","F70-1218","F70-1313","F70-1364","F70-1445","F70-1647","F70-1747","F70-1786","F70-1869"],"countries":{"GB":8,"JP":8,"AU":1}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"steering","theme":"Multi-function steering wheel operation","frequency":3,"likes":1,"wants":0,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":2,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["nice little car but it did take me a fair while to get my head around all the tech, i prefer things very plain and simple and as an older driver it felt a bit of a slog at the start. i specced the car with almost every extra i could get, as thats what i tend to do. now i am really pleased with it, the way it clings to the road is like a limpet and the steering gives loads of feedback, it almost feels like the car is talking to me and i always feel totally in control. over the years ive had around seven bmws, mostly three series and a couple of x2, and this one is every bit as good as those.","driving itself is good. voice control is poor, you have to say things exactly right so you end up watching the screen instead of the road. the steering wheel audio controls are useless, you can only scroll the playlist one track at a time, and mine is huge, so to pick a song i go back to the main screen, again not looking at the road. don't like the tiny fuel gauge low on the left, and i really miss the door handle lighting","why is there a character limit? mechanically it feels cheap, rushed and badly tuned, not what i expected from bmw. my old 2010 e82 1 series was superior in every respect. the missing idrive wheel is a letdown and there is no proper replacement. mercedes puts a touch pad on the steering wheel, but here both next track buttons are inconsistent and irritating to use. the suspension needs more tuning for uk motorways and roads. the hybrid system also needs a lot of work: when you come up to a roundabout it sits in too high a gear and takes about two seconds to change down. i picked the bmw hybrid "],"feedbackIds":["F70-0009","F70-0739","F70-1585"],"countries":{"GB":3}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"exterior","theme":"Comfort Access","frequency":3,"likes":0,"wants":0,"difficultToUse":2,"defect":1,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["its a really good car, definitely feels like an upgrade over my old f40 118i m sport. engine is strong and the mild hybrid gives a nice extra shove and helps with efficiency. it corners and rides very well and im getting better fuel economy than with the f40. some of the cabin materials feel a bit flimsier than before, not a big deal but i did notice. the new cabin layout looks great and all the digital stuff behaves properly. a few oddities though: the keyless entry/exit reacts way too easily, and sometimes the car systems seem to randomly reset, so auto hold ends up switched off in the menu ","it feels overly complicated. drives really well but honestly they should remove most of the tech. the keyless door entry is a real nuisance... i dont think a car needs all this technology.","i wish it had a boot close button and also proper keyless entry."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0010","F70-1166","F70-1563"],"countries":{"GB":3}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"engine","theme":"Drivetrain","frequency":548,"likes":427,"wants":17,"difficultToUse":82,"defect":22,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["its a really good car, definitely feels like an upgrade over my old f40 118i m sport. engine is strong and the mild hybrid gives a nice extra shove and helps with efficiency. it corners and rides very well and im getting better fuel economy than with the f40. some of the cabin materials feel a bit flimsier than before, not a big deal but i did notice. the new cabin layout looks great and all the digital stuff behaves properly. a few oddities though: the keyless entry/exit reacts way too easily, and sometimes the car systems seem to randomly reset, so auto hold ends up switched off in the menu ","driving feel that makes you forget its front wheel drive.\r\ncomes fully loaded with on-board gear.","the mileage is good and the interior is also good.","this is my 4th bmw 1 series and easily the best to drive. the mild hybrid setup is excellent, same with the automatic gearbox. i have already done around a 1000 mile round trip to france in great comfort and with superb fuel economy.","the car drives well and is comfortable with plenty of space. i'm still getting my head around the technical features, mainly because i haven't been in the car much thanks to a health issue. i do like the stylish appearance of the car.","i absolutely love this car, it rides so smoothly and is really comfortable. the performance is terrific all round. it was always my dream car and still is, and it does not let me down in any part."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0010","F70-0019","F70-0023","F70-0028","F70-0032","F70-0033","F70-0038","F70-0039","F70-0042","F70-0043","F70-0049","F70-0050","F70-0052","F70-0059","F70-0063","F70-0066","F70-0067","F70-0071","F70-0077","F70-0081","F70-0086","F70-0087","F70-0091","F70-0093","F70-0094","F70-0095","F70-0095","F70-0096","F70-0098","F70-0104"],"countries":{"GB":284,"JP":239,"KR":3,"SE":13,"AU":3,"FR":6}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"interior","theme":"Interior design","frequency":29,"likes":26,"wants":3,"difficultToUse":0,"defect":0,"none":0,"sampleVerbatims":["its a really good car, definitely feels like an upgrade over my old f40 118i m sport. engine is strong and the mild hybrid gives a nice extra shove and helps with efficiency. it corners and rides very well and im getting better fuel economy than with the f40. some of the cabin materials feel a bit flimsier than before, not a big deal but i did notice. the new cabin layout looks great and all the digital stuff behaves properly. a few oddities though: the keyless entry/exit reacts way too easily, and sometimes the car systems seem to randomly reset, so auto hold ends up switched off in the menu ","i used to own an m135i, and that one was much more fun to drive, mainly because the exhaust sounded fantastic. the new m135 has almost no sound and feels boring to drive, even though the new interior is really well done.","very good-looking car, modern interior with features that fit that modern style.","i changed from the 3 series because of the parking space, but even though this is smaller and narrower it doesn't feel tight inside, and it is quick on its feet and has enough power. i really liked the instrument panel design, it looks upscale and is easy to read. i chose the m sport and i'm also pleased with the suspension and the audio. i think it is recommendable for people who want good fuel economy and do not like driving something big.","the inside looks great and the outside is just as impressive. power, safety, everyday convenience and the whole user interface setup are all spot on. as a compact car it feels almost perfectly put together.","really lovely looking car, with an interior and tech that are very impressive. feels much nicer all round than the earlier model."],"feedbackIds":["F70-0010","F70-0045","F70-0056","F70-0095","F70-0153","F70-0297","F70-0300","F70-0345","F70-0350","F70-0425","F70-0661","F70-0706","F70-0777","F70-0927","F70-0982","F70-1021","F70-1121","F70-1337","F70-1356","F70-1523","F70-1573","F70-1672","F70-1676","F70-1704","F70-1848","F70-1918","F70-2033","F70-2093","F70-2120"],"countries":{"GB":21,"JP":7,"SE":1}},{"vehicleCode":"F70","component":"steering","theme":"Speed Limit Assistant","frequency":7,"likes":0,"wants":0,"difficultToUse":5,"defect

